\details{
Read \code{Question} and \code{UseWhen}, then open the help for \code{MainFunction}.
\code{TypicalInput} identifies the required object and \code{NextStep} its continuation.
\code{DecisionBoundary} and \code{Notes} describe the limit of the route; a listed
function does not imply that every model can use it.

The five default routes are choices, not required stages. G/D planning uses
observed ratings without an MFRM fit. Explicit \code{"public"} and \code{"beginner"}
retain the six-row ordinary RSM/PCM route. Other scopes select a topic or
output family. Names ending in \verb{_table}, \verb{_report}, \verb{_review} or \verb{_bundle}
describe the role of the result, not interchangeable input classes.
